        {
          "id": "3912425587263874733",
          "shortcode": "DZLule7Ayat",
          "timestamp": 1780617558,
          "caption": "The most expensive mistake I almost made wasn’t choosing the wrong path…\n\nIt was staying on it.\n\nMost of us have had that feeling where we know deep down something isn’t right—whether it’s a career, relationship, or people you’ve outgrown. But we ignore that feeling and keep pushing through.\n\nThis quote reminds us that the longer you convince yourself that this is what you want or that it’s “too late” to change paths, the harder it is to course correct. \n\nBecause every stop adds another reason to stay. More time invested. More money invested. More milestones to walk away from.\n\nFor me, that train was law.\n\nI spent my whole life working to become a lawyer, and when I finally did, it was nothing like I imagined. I was miserable. So, I left right after I got licensed. Some people might say I quit too soon, that I didn’t give it a real shot. My parents even begged me to work for another year to be sure. But I refused, because I knew my mind wouldn’t change and staying would only make the inevitable decision more difficult. It’s been a year and I honestly have no regrets. \n\nI’ve also learned that no matter how long you’ve been on the wrong train, it’s never truly “too late” to get off. The fare may be higher. The journey back may take longer. But if you stay on the wrong train forever... you’ll never get home.\n  What’s a train you’ve been thinking about getting off?\n\n#lawyer #corporategirl #careerchange #quityourjob #hopecore",
